  "title": "Book of Dede Korkut",
  "summary": "The Book of Dede Korkut is a collection of Oghuz Turkic tales. The Dresden manuscript, a prologue plus twelve tales, is likely a sixteenth-century copy of an older text. A shorter Vatican manuscript with about half the stories turned up later. The text was first printed in Turkish in 1916.",
